{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 41,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David. Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that considereth the poor: the LORD will deliver him in the time of trouble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he shall be blessed upon the earth: and thou wilt not deliver him to the will of his enemies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD will strengthen him upon the bed of languishing: thou wilt make all his bed in his sickness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said, LORD, be merciful to me: heal my soul; for I have sinned against thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My enemies speak evil of me, When shall he die, and his name perish?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if he cometh to see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he speaketh vanity: his heart gathereth iniquity to itself; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he goeth abroad, he telleth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All that hate me whisper together against me: against me do they devise my hurt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An evil disease, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "say they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", cleaveth fast to him: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "now",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that he lieth he shall rise no more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, my own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, who ate of my bread, hath lifted up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " heel against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou, O LORD, be merciful to me, and raise me up, that I may requite them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By this I know that thou favorest me, because my enemy doth not triumph over me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as for me, thou upholdest me in my integrity, and settest me before thy face for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.41.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.41.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. Amen, and amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
